What is a firewall?
A firewall is a security system that controls incoming and outgoing network traffic according to rules.

Imagine your Ubuntu server has several services:
- SSH – port 22
- HTTP – port 80
- HTTPS – port 443
- Spark or Hadoop services – their configured ports
You may want to allow SSH from trusted sources while blocking unnecessary connections.
